# Supabase project settings (Project Settings -> API)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only. Used by the Supabase admin client for Storage signed URL work if needed.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Server-only, and only needed to run `npm run migrate` (scripts/migrate.mjs)
# instead of pasting each supabase/migrations/*.sql file into the Supabase
# SQL editor by hand. Get it from Supabase -> Project Settings -> Database ->
# Connection string ("URI"); use the DIRECT connection on port 5432, not the
# pgbouncer pooler on 6543. Never commit the real value — this is a full
# Postgres superuser-ish credential, not a scoped API key.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:your-db-password@db.your-project.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# Server-only. Never exposed to the client. Used by app/api/claude/* routes.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Server-only. Optional — only needed for the Rooms/Interior Design/Landscape
# tabs' "Generate image (AI)" button (lib/gemini.ts), which calls Google's
# Gemini API (Gemini 3 Pro Image, aka "Nano Banana Pro" — the Pro tier,
# chosen for higher detail/accuracy than the Flash tier previously used,
# at a real cost/latency tradeoff) to render or redesign-in-place a
# room/exterior photo automatically instead of you pasting the prompt
# into an image tool by hand. Get a key at aistudio.google.com/apikey.
# Without this set, the app still writes a concise image prompt you can
# copy elsewhere — it just won't generate the image itself.
GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# Optional — overrides the Gemini model id in lib/gemini.ts without a code
# change (e.g. "gemini-3.1-flash-image" to fall back to the cheaper/faster
# Flash tier if Pro's cost/latency isn't worth it, or to correct the
# default if Google renames/GAs the Pro preview id below).
# GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3-pro-image-preview

# Server-only. Optional — only needed for the "Get alerts" button on each
# construction (lib/email.ts, lib/alerts.ts), which emails subscribers on
# chat messages, checklist/warranty item updates, and warranty status
# changes. Every alert email includes a one-click unsubscribe link
# (app/api/alerts/unsubscribe/route.ts). Get a key at resend.com — the free
# tier is 3,000 emails/month. Without this set, subscribing still works but
# no email actually sends (the failure is logged, not shown to the user —
# see lib/alerts.ts).
RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# Server-only. Optional — the "from" address alert emails are sent from.
# Defaults to Resend's shared "onboarding@resend.dev", which only delivers
# to the account owner's own verified email — fine for testing this
# yourself, not for real subscribers. Verify a domain in Resend's dashboard
# and set this to an address on it (e.g. alerts@yourdomain.com) before
# relying on this for anyone else.
ALERT_FROM_EMAIL=alerts@yourdomain.com

# Optional — Web Push notifications (components/PushNotificationToggle.tsx,
# lib/webPush.ts), sent alongside the email alerts above whenever someone
# who's both subscribed to a construction's alerts AND enabled push on a
# device would otherwise only get an email. Generate a keypair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`. NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY is not a
# secret (it has to reach the browser to subscribe) — VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY is,
# never commit the real value. Without both set, the "Enable notifications"
# button on the Constructions page never appears.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=...
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=...
# Optional — a contact the push service can reach if it needs to reach you
# about your usage (a mailto: or https: URL). Defaults to a placeholder.
VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@yourdomain.com
